 "notes": "Axion haloscope (lumped-element superconducting LC circuit). Headline curve is the blue \"90% Limit, RFI Limit\" (the actual measured exclusion given observed RFI excesses) from FIG. 4 panels b/c/d (limit_1.png, limit_2a.png, limit_2b.png in the e-print), covering three narrow mass windows at B=4.5,5.0,7.0 T. The orange \"90% Limit without RFI estimated\" curve (an estimate of what could be achieved if RFI candidates were removed) is NOT reported. Figures are raster PNGs; curve read by pixel extraction with tick calibration (x log-free freq axis, y log10 coupling; verified endpoints against abstract mass ranges 1.7498-1.7519e-7, 1.7734-1.7738e-7, 1.8007-1.8015e-7 eV). Frequency converted to mass via m_a = h*f (h=4.1357e-15 eV*s), reproducing the paper stated eV values. Vertical scan-edge walls (rising to the ~1e-10 CAST ceiling) trimmed. Coupling axis label \"Coupling (GeV^-1)\" = g_agamma in L=-g a E.B, equivalent to the canonical L=-(g/4)aFFdual. The paper does not state an assumed local dark-matter density, so dm_density_assumed is null (the limit does depend on density but no value is given).",
